1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,500
Hollywood Leading Ladies — Then & Now

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,288
Welcome to Hollywood Leading Ladies, Then and
Now.

3
00:00:15,388 --> 00:00:22,488
Julia Roberts became a global favorite with
Pretty Woman, then gave Erin Brockovich a sharp,
determined center.

4
00:00:22,588 --> 00:00:27,570
Across the years, her famous smile still carries
both comedy and conviction.

5
00:00:27,670 --> 00:00:33,076
Angelina Jolie has moved between action
spectacle, intimate drama, directing, and
humanitarian work.

6
00:00:33,176 --> 00:00:40,275
Lara Croft, Girl Interrupted, and Maleficent show
only a few of the contrasting images in her
career.

7
00:00:40,375 --> 00:00:44,511
Nicole Kidman has made reinvention part of her
screen language.

8
00:00:44,611 --> 00:00:54,251
From Moulin Rouge to The Hours, The Others, and
Big Little Lies, she can make glamour, suspense,
and quiet vulnerability feel equally precise.

9
00:00:54,351 --> 00:01:01,128
Compare the early and recent portraits and notice
how each actress has reshaped a familiar image.

10
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:03,000
Three more icons. Look closely at the portraits and the roles that made them familiar.

11
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:06,621
The next three leading ladies carry that story
forward.

12
00:04:06,721 --> 00:04:13,648
Kate Winslet made Rose unforgettable in Titanic,
then kept seeking complicated characters in films
and television dramas.

13
00:04:13,748 --> 00:04:17,369
Her work often feels lived in rather than posed.

14
00:04:17,469 --> 00:04:28,944
Charlize Theron has crossed from the dramatic
transformation of Monster to the physical force
of Mad Max Fury Road, proving that range can be
both emotional and athletic.

15
00:04:29,044 --> 00:04:34,732
Anne Hathaway first introduced many viewers to a
shy princess in The Princess Diaries.

16
00:04:34,832 --> 00:04:43,000
Later roles in The Devil Wears Prada, Les
Miserables, and Interstellar revealed a performer
comfortable with wit, music, and depth.

17
00:04:43,100 --> 00:04:45,067
Six portraits, six evolving careers.

18
00:04:45,167 --> 00:04:50,128
Which role appears in your mind the moment you
see each face?

19
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:59,700
Which early and later pairing surprised you most?
